{"id":"d06ac5a66d69d291","group":"58","path":"58/batch15/58-df-forcing.md","title":"Forcing","display":"df-forcing — Forcing","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-forcing","aliases":["58-df-forcing"],"display":"df-forcing — Forcing","depends_on":["[[58-df-poset]]","[[58-df-ctm]]","[[58-df-filter]]","[[58-df-name]]","[[58-df-name-evaluation]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-forcing"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-forcing</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-forcing — Forcing"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"d3f859dbdd37f018\" href=\"?note=d3f859dbdd37f018\" title=\"58-df-poset\">58-df-poset</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"66d43bb76d055059\" href=\"?note=66d43bb76d055059\" title=\"58-df-ctm\">58-df-ctm</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"1331244a5201bb99\" href=\"?note=1331244a5201bb99\" title=\"58-df-filter\">58-df-filter</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"ec28b62254928d73\" href=\"?note=ec28b62254928d73\" title=\"58-df-name\">58-df-name</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"0c40d420e5118724\" href=\"?note=0c40d420e5118724\" title=\"58-df-name-evaluation\">58-df-name-evaluation</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Gamma\\subseteq\\mathrm{Fml}_S\">\\(\\Gamma\\subseteq\\mathrm{Fml}_S\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\Gamma)\">\\(\\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\Gamma)\\)</span> (countable transitive model, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"66d43bb76d055059\" href=\"?note=66d43bb76d055059\" title=\"58-df-ctm\">58-df-ctm</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P,R\\in M\">\\(P,R\\in M\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Poset}(P,R)\">\\(\\mathrm{Poset}(P,R)\\)</span> (forcing poset, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"d3f859dbdd37f018\" href=\"?note=d3f859dbdd37f018\" title=\"58-df-poset\">58-df-poset</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"G\\subseteq P\">\\(G\\subseteq P\\)</span> (<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M\">\\(M\\)</span>-generic filter)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Name}(\\dot x,P)\">\\(\\mathrm{Name}(\\dot x,P)\\)</span> (<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P\">\\(P\\)</span>-name in <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M\">\\(M\\)</span>, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"ec28b62254928d73\" href=\"?note=ec28b62254928d73\" title=\"58-df-name\">58-df-name</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{val}_{G,P}(\\dot x)\">\\(\\operatorname{val}_{G,P}(\\dot x)\\)</span> (interpretation of a name by <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"G\">\\(G\\)</span>, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"0c40d420e5118724\" href=\"?note=0c40d420e5118724\" title=\"58-df-name-evaluation\">58-df-name-evaluation</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MGenericFilter}_S(G,M,P,R)\">\\(\\mathrm{MGenericFilter}_S(G,M,P,R)\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ForcingSetup}_S(M,\\Gamma,P,R,G)\">\\(\\mathrm{ForcingSetup}_S(M,\\Gamma,P,R,G)\\)</span> (predicates defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}forcing\\text{-}generic}\\vdash \\mathrm{MGenericFilter}_S(G,M,P,R)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Filter}_S(G,P,R)\\land\\forall D\\in M\\;\\left(\\left[D\\subseteq P\\land\\forall p\\in P\\;\\exists d\\in D\\;(\\langle d,p\\rangle\\in R)\\right]\\to G\\cap D\\neq\\varnothing\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}forcing\\text{-}generic}\\vdash \\mathrm{MGenericFilter}_S(G,M,P,R)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Filter}_S(G,P,R)\\land\\forall D\\in M\\;\\left(\\left[D\\subseteq P\\land\\forall p\\in P\\;\\exists d\\in D\\;(\\langle d,p\\rangle\\in R)\\right]\\to G\\cap D\\neq\\varnothing\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}forcing\\text{-}setup} \\vdash \\mathrm{ForcingSetup}_S(M,\\Gamma,P,R,G)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\Gamma)\\land\\langle P,R\\rangle\\in M\\land\\mathrm{Poset}(P,R)\\land\\mathrm{MGenericFilter}_S(G,M,P,R)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}forcing\\text{-}setup} \\vdash \\mathrm{ForcingSetup}_S(M,\\Gamma,P,R,G)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\Gamma)\\land\\langle P,R\\rangle\\in M\\land\\mathrm{Poset}(P,R)\\land\\mathrm{MGenericFilter}_S(G,M,P,R)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}forcing\\text{-}extension} \\vdash \\mathrm{ForcingSetup}_S(M,\\Gamma,P,R,G)\\to M[G]_P\\coloneqq\\{\\operatorname{val}_{G,P}(\\dot x):\\dot x\\in M\\land\\mathrm{Name}(\\dot x,P)\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}forcing\\text{-}extension} \\vdash \\mathrm{ForcingSetup}_S(M,\\Gamma,P,R,G)\\to M[G]_P\\coloneqq\\{\\operatorname{val}_{G,P}(\\dot x):\\dot x\\in M\\land\\mathrm{Name}(\\dot x,P)\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Forcing is a technique for constructing models of set theory</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M[G]\">\\(M[G]\\)</span> is the generic extension obtained by adding a generic filter <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"G \\subseteq P\">\\(G \\subseteq P\\)</span></li>\n<li>The names are exactly the members of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M\">\\(M\\)</span> satisfying the rank-recursive predicate <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Name}(-,P)\">\\(\\mathrm{Name}(-,P)\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-poset","status":"resolved","id":"d3f859dbdd37f018","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-poset]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-ctm","status":"resolved","id":"66d43bb76d055059","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-ctm]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-filter","status":"resolved","id":"1331244a5201bb99","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-filter]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-name","status":"resolved","id":"ec28b62254928d73","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-name]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-name-evaluation","status":"resolved","id":"0c40d420e5118724","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-name-evaluation]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-ctm","status":"resolved","id":"66d43bb76d055059","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\Gamma\\subseteq\\mathrm{Fml}_S$ and $\\mathrm{CTM}_S(M,\\Gamma)$ (countable transitive model, see [[58-df-ctm]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-poset","status":"resolved","id":"d3f859dbdd37f018","anchor":"ref-7","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$P,R\\in M$ and $\\math